      ],
      "words": 31
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Marry me,” he said suddenly. “Lucia, we should be married.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7418
        },
        {
          "text": "“They’re unlikely to draft me if I am. We can run away together, far away, some other place.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7522
        }
      ],
      "words": 29
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“But then I will be married to you, and I will die a happier man,” he insisted",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7747
        }
      ],
      "words": 17
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "In this moment, an electric current ran through me. It numbed my limbs, my face, my feelings. I saw the depths and I ran",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8540
        }
      ],
      "words": 24
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I wanted to find him",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9077
        },
        {
          "text": "To hold him",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9099
        },
        {
          "text": "But the only thing left was a perverse shadow of his image",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9112
        }
      ],
      "words": 22
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The funny thing about grief was you knew they were gone. There was not one possible way that it could be them. In dreams",
